<headroom-library version="1" id="hg-clean-dirty-stomp" category="High Gain" order="160" instrument="guitar" style="Nu Metal">
  <description>Quiet-loud nu metal in one rig: a hard gate in front of a solid-state chorus clean and a tight early rectified head side by side. Ride the Clean/Dirty macro from creepy chorused verse arpeggios to gated stop-start riffs; the gate snaps every hit shut.</description>
  <tags><tag>High Gain</tag><tag>Nu Metal</tag><tag>Rhythm</tag><tag>Gate</tag><tag>Clean</tag><tag>Dynamic</tag><tag>Stop-Start</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.premierguitar.com/gear/rig-rundown-korn" title="Premier Guitar: Rig Rundown, Korn"/>
    <source url="https://www.musicradar.com/news/guitars/slipknots-mick-thomson-and-jim-root-talk-gear-tone-and-being-flat-broke-580682" title="MusicRadar: Slipknot's Mick Thomson and Jim Root talk gear"/>
    <source url="https://equipboard.com/posts/the-best-noise-gate-pedals" title="Equipboard: The best noise gate pedals"/>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesa/Boogie_Rectifier" title="Mesa/Boogie Rectifier (Wikipedia)"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
